1
00:00:00,292 --> 00:00:02,962
Why didn't you tell me
that happened to you?

2
00:00:03,045 --> 00:00:06,006
What, you think we can't protect you?

3
00:00:06,257 --> 00:00:07,800
I don't want to be a burden.

4
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:09,301
You probably think…

5
00:00:09,385 --> 00:00:10,386
I'm weak.

6
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:16,225
I'm doing all of this
because I love you all so much.

7
00:00:18,394 --> 00:00:20,604
It was your brother who gave me orders.

8
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:23,232
-It was Georgia who did it?
-That's not true!

9
00:00:23,607 --> 00:00:25,651
-Don't push me, Georgia.
-Come on!

10
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,236
I fight back.

11
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:29,029
Your full payment.

12
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,990
You want to silence me
about what happened?

13
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,700
I thought that's what you wanted.

14
00:00:33,075 --> 00:00:35,035
It's so easy for you
to give up on me, isn't it?

15
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:36,495
Well…

16
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:39,123
you never defended me, anyway.

17
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:41,625
Maybe I really don't know…

18
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:43,586
how to be a good mother.

19
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:48,257
If only Patricia knew… I'm trying…

20
00:00:49,425 --> 00:00:51,594
You're getting a little too casual
with me now.

21
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:52,803
Is that a bad thing?

22
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,346
Just don't get used to it.

23
00:00:54,638 --> 00:00:56,557
We're strictly co-workers.

24
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,225
I'm already gaining her trust.

25
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:01,228
I'll avenge you.

26
00:01:07,026 --> 00:01:09,779
Boss, he's the one I told you about.

27
00:01:12,323 --> 00:01:14,575
You're Ricardo Salvador's former coworker?

28
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:16,368
Yes.

29
00:01:16,452 --> 00:01:17,661
What is this about?

30
00:01:18,162 --> 00:01:19,747
How long did you work together?

31
00:01:20,623 --> 00:01:22,500
About a year.

32
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,460
He'd just returned to the Philippines.

33
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:26,253
What was he like?

34
00:01:26,796 --> 00:01:28,172
He was good.

35
00:01:28,506 --> 00:01:31,050
The truth is, he was really good
at what he did.

36
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:34,303
He was smart, always had a solution,

37
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:36,555
and had incredible powers of persuasion.

38
00:01:37,056 --> 00:01:39,975
That's why he was the biggest asset
at our PR firm.

39
00:01:40,059 --> 00:01:41,352
-All right, that's enough.
-That's why he kept getting promoted…

40
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:43,354
Get to the point. What was wrong with him?

41
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:47,107
-Wrong with him?
-Yes. What was wrong with him?

42
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:51,570
Did he have any vices? Any enemies?

43
00:01:52,071 --> 00:01:53,656
Did he do anything wrong?

44
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:57,076
Or was there anything strange
or suspicious about him?

45
00:01:58,035 --> 00:02:01,622
You know, Ricardo got along with everyone.

46
00:02:02,748 --> 00:02:05,835
We just didn't really hang out
with him when we went out.

47
00:02:06,293 --> 00:02:07,711
Only at events,

48
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:10,297
but those were part of the job.

49
00:02:10,798 --> 00:02:12,716
When it was time to go home,

50
00:02:13,217 --> 00:02:14,927
he'd head straight home.

51
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:18,097
Whenever we'd talk about our families,

52
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:20,766
he never really mentioned anything.

53
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:25,563
We'd complain about our parents,

54
00:02:25,855 --> 00:02:30,526
our in-laws,
issues with our spouses, our kids.

55
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:33,779
But Ricardo…

56
00:02:34,947 --> 00:02:36,240
I can't remember anything.

57
00:02:39,410 --> 00:02:44,123
You mean, none of you
ever met his wife or child?

58
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:45,875
Not once.

59
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:49,336
He never told us anything personal.

60
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,046
If he had a family,

61
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:53,465
we never met them.

62
00:02:54,258 --> 00:02:58,053
We just thought
he was a very private person.

63
00:02:58,888 --> 00:03:01,640
I can't remember any coworker

64
00:03:01,724 --> 00:03:03,809
who became really close to Ricardo.

65
00:03:04,435 --> 00:03:06,145
He didn't talk about himself.

66
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:07,730
It was always just work.

67
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,181
Sir, everything's ready.

68
00:03:43,098 --> 00:03:44,141
Okay, do it.

69
00:05:22,239 --> 00:05:23,866
Whose house is this?

70
00:05:26,368 --> 00:05:29,496
What are we doing here?
Why did you bring me here?

71
00:05:45,554 --> 00:05:47,097
This piano…

72
00:05:57,191 --> 00:05:58,442
That's Mom.

73
00:06:01,737 --> 00:06:04,073
That's Teddy and me when we were kids.

74
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:06,700
Whose house is this, really?

75
00:06:08,619 --> 00:06:10,704
You have so many questions about your mom.

76
00:06:10,788 --> 00:06:12,539
I just want to help you find the answers.

77
00:06:15,334 --> 00:06:16,960
Why did you bring me here?

78
00:06:18,629 --> 00:06:20,380
To answer your questions.

79
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:22,800
Your mom lived here.

80
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:26,053
I spoke to one of your father's
former employees.

81
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:30,099
He said your mom lived here
until she got sick.

82
00:06:30,182 --> 00:06:31,475
She died here too.

83
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:33,018
Until the very end,

84
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:35,687
you and your brother were
the only ones on her mind.

85
00:06:38,524 --> 00:06:40,109
Your mom lived here for a long time.

86
00:06:40,192 --> 00:06:42,069
Except for the caretaker,

87
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:46,156
she didn't interact with anyone.

88
00:06:47,491 --> 00:06:49,243
Not since she left your family.

89
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:52,246
Dad didn't want us talking about her.

90
00:06:53,247 --> 00:06:55,249
He always took me to La Familia

91
00:06:55,332 --> 00:06:57,459
so I wouldn't look for Mom.

92
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:01,964
That's why I never got
to experience being a child.

93
00:07:05,092 --> 00:07:06,593
Do you know why she disappeared?

94
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:10,055
People used to say she'd left
with another man.

95
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:14,977
Diana.

96
00:07:18,605 --> 00:07:20,107
According to the records,

97
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:23,193
that man had already been living
in America for years.

98
00:07:23,485 --> 00:07:25,821
The same year your mom left your family.

99
00:07:30,159 --> 00:07:32,786
She wanted to come back to you,
but Don Lucio did everything he could

100
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:34,413
to keep her from coming back.

101
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:38,959
Thank you.

102
00:07:40,377 --> 00:07:41,837
Your mom developed depression

103
00:07:42,421 --> 00:07:43,839
after she gave birth to Teddy.

104
00:07:44,256 --> 00:07:45,757
It might have been postpartum depression.

105
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:48,635
But she shut herself away in this house

106
00:07:48,719 --> 00:07:49,928
and withdrew from the world.

107
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:56,476
All this time, I never knew
why Mom did that.

108
00:07:57,895 --> 00:08:02,649
She was so tender and loving.

109
00:08:05,027 --> 00:08:05,944
And…

110
00:08:06,445 --> 00:08:08,238
she was into the arts.

111
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,116
She taught me how to play the piano.

112
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:13,410
I have so many questions.

113
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:20,042
Did she get tired of being our mother?

114
00:08:22,169 --> 00:08:24,213
Was I not enough for her?

115
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:27,966
But I should've gone after her.

116
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:31,178
Maybe I did something wrong.

117
00:08:34,181 --> 00:08:36,808
I failed her so much as her daughter.

118
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:47,444
Why are you doing this, Ricardo?

119
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:56,161
So you can finally get answers
to all the questions you've been carrying.

120
00:08:57,162 --> 00:08:58,997
So you can finally have peace.

121
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:26,233
Oh.

122
00:09:26,775 --> 00:09:29,319
Come on now. Please don't do this.

123
00:09:29,403 --> 00:09:32,364
I need you to work.
I've still got a lot to do. Come on.

124
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:38,787
That won't answer back.

125
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:41,498
Let me.

126
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:43,792
You seem all worked up from multitasking.

127
00:09:45,043 --> 00:09:46,003
You've no idea.

128
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:48,171
I need at least ten hands.

129
00:09:48,547 --> 00:09:50,007
Or maybe a twin.

130
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,967
Someone who can help me around here.

131
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,054
Ta-da!

132
00:09:56,138 --> 00:09:58,181
You fixed it? Wow.

133
00:09:58,265 --> 00:09:59,391
It's working now.

134
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:01,268
Nice. Thanks.

135
00:10:07,983 --> 00:10:08,817
You're going back to school?

136
00:10:09,776 --> 00:10:10,902
That's good, Patricia.

137
00:10:12,571 --> 00:10:14,990
If I pass the entrance exam.

138
00:10:16,575 --> 00:10:18,493
-Does Ms. D know?
-Hey.

139
00:10:18,577 --> 00:10:21,496
What does she have to do with this?
She doesn't need to know.

140
00:10:21,872 --> 00:10:23,415
I got this.

141
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:26,501
I will pay my tuition fee.

142
00:10:27,336 --> 00:10:31,089
And I think I can study

143
00:10:31,173 --> 00:10:32,758
and work here at the same time.

144
00:10:33,258 --> 00:10:36,011
I'll help you. I am a good tutor.

145
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:38,513
I'm not a child.

146
00:10:38,597 --> 00:10:39,681
I'm in college.

147
00:10:40,057 --> 00:10:41,266
This is easy-peasy.

148
00:10:42,309 --> 00:10:43,435
Besides…

149
00:10:44,269 --> 00:10:45,520
I don't want you to be my tutor.

150
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:48,523
You stress me out when you're being…

151
00:10:50,108 --> 00:10:51,109
meticulous.

152
00:10:52,319 --> 00:10:53,445
Oh, wow.

153
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:55,655
-Meticulous?
-Mm-hmm.

154
00:10:57,032 --> 00:10:59,785
You're really not used
to asking for help, are you?

155
00:11:01,453 --> 00:11:02,579
You already know the answer.

156
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:04,289
Hmm.

157
00:11:04,873 --> 00:11:07,334
I'll still help you.
You don't have a choice.

158
00:11:17,052 --> 00:11:19,012
Jena, April.

159
00:11:19,096 --> 00:11:21,223
Come here. I've something to ask.

160
00:11:22,933 --> 00:11:23,934
What is it, Dad?

161
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,102
Jena.

162
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:27,104
Do you know how to sell online?

163
00:11:27,813 --> 00:11:28,897
You mean live selling?

164
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,524
Yes, exactly.

165
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:33,777
I'd like to sell my products
on the internet.

166
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:34,820
How do I start?

167
00:11:34,903 --> 00:11:37,280
It's easy, Dad. Here. Give me your phone.

168
00:11:37,364 --> 00:11:39,282
We will create and register your account.

169
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:40,659
Here.

170
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:43,578
Dad, are you sure you can do it?

171
00:11:44,079 --> 00:11:45,163
Absolutely.

172
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:49,000
A lot of our neighbors do it.

173
00:11:50,085 --> 00:11:53,505
They sell all kinds of stuff
and earn a lot.

174
00:11:53,588 --> 00:11:56,716
My soaps and vitamins
are different from the rest.

175
00:11:57,426 --> 00:11:58,468
And come on,

176
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,971
you have a handsome dad.

177
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:03,098
Do you really think
no one will buy from me?

178
00:12:03,181 --> 00:12:05,600
Wow! I love the confidence!

179
00:12:05,684 --> 00:12:07,644
Impressive.

180
00:12:08,478 --> 00:12:10,897
I'm tired of being belittled.

181
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:15,569
I want to prove them wrong.

182
00:12:19,114 --> 00:12:20,198
Hey, how's my account?

183
00:12:20,282 --> 00:12:22,284
I got you. It's almost done, Dad.

184
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:23,452
Hurry up.

185
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:32,127
-Found you.
-Hmm! Why?

186
00:12:33,712 --> 00:12:34,713
What's that?

187
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:36,631
Notes from the Burger City
marketing meeting.

188
00:12:37,299 --> 00:12:38,758
Why are you giving it to me?

189
00:12:38,842 --> 00:12:43,388
Ms. D wants you to help her plan
a new campaign for Burger City.

190
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:49,769
Why me?

191
00:12:50,687 --> 00:12:51,771
I don't know either.

192
00:12:51,855 --> 00:12:53,523
She didn't tell me.

193
00:12:54,024 --> 00:12:56,109
Maybe because
you're new here in La Familia.

194
00:12:56,568 --> 00:12:58,612
Maybe for fresh insights?

195
00:12:58,987 --> 00:13:00,197
Hmm.

196
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:04,117
None of my ideas are fresh
with all the work I have to do.

197
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:08,455
I don't know, Patricia.

198
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:11,500
Maybe it's because
she's reaching out to you.

199
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:13,168
Or maybe…

200
00:13:13,251 --> 00:13:15,378
it's because she trusts you.

201
00:13:15,837 --> 00:13:19,049
Why don't you just tell her
that you'll go back to school?

202
00:13:24,679 --> 00:13:26,264
What if I don't pass the test?

203
00:13:27,224 --> 00:13:30,602
I'm just adding to her list
of disappointments.

204
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:32,062
Hmm?

205
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:34,356
You said you can do it, right?

206
00:13:34,439 --> 00:13:36,274
-Hmm?
-You can do it.

207
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:37,901
"I love my life."

208
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:40,529
Oh, great.

209
00:13:40,612 --> 00:13:42,906
Really now? Are we that close?

210
00:13:43,782 --> 00:13:45,534
Stop worrying.

211
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:48,119
I'll help you with that.

212
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,747
Just call me, okay?

213
00:14:00,090 --> 00:14:02,008
-I can do it.
-Good.

214
00:14:03,969 --> 00:14:07,389
I love my life. I love my life.
I love my life.

215
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:08,932
Hey, later, okay?

216
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:10,684
I'll help you study.

217
00:14:16,565 --> 00:14:19,859
Five pesos
for each correct answer you'll get.

218
00:14:20,986 --> 00:14:24,072
Well, be prepared to lose all your coins.

219
00:14:29,536 --> 00:14:30,579
Wrong.

220
00:14:30,662 --> 00:14:31,788
Darn it.

221
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:34,541
Nineteen, A.

222
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:36,042
-Correct.
-Yes!

223
00:14:39,045 --> 00:14:40,880
-Hey!
-Time to review.

224
00:14:41,339 --> 00:14:42,591
I need to finish this.

225
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:44,759
You have to be disciplined with your time.

226
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:46,845
If you have time for La Familia,

227
00:14:46,928 --> 00:14:48,513
you should also have time to study.

228
00:14:48,597 --> 00:14:51,266
Because that's the only way
we get to accomplish this.

229
00:14:51,349 --> 00:14:52,100
Wrong!

230
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:53,560
-Wrong?
-Wrong.

231
00:14:55,312 --> 00:14:56,521
Just do it.

232
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:02,360
The correct answer is…

233
00:15:02,444 --> 00:15:04,112
-A.
-Yay!

234
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:05,905
Jackpot!

235
00:15:05,989 --> 00:15:07,866
Mm-hmm. Jackpot.

236
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:10,410
I hit the jackpot with your mistakes.

237
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:11,828
Hmm.

238
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,413
You got a lot wrong.

239
00:15:15,624 --> 00:15:19,085
-Happy birthday to you
-Give me that.

240
00:15:19,169 --> 00:15:21,129
You're really not used
to asking for help, huh?

241
00:15:21,963 --> 00:15:22,881
Happy birthday

242
00:15:22,964 --> 00:15:26,426
Happy birthday, happy birthday

243
00:15:26,509 --> 00:15:29,512
Happy birthday to you

244
00:15:29,596 --> 00:15:32,390
Happy birthday!

245
00:15:32,474 --> 00:15:34,517
They're so sweet with their mom.

246
00:15:36,186 --> 00:15:37,520
A family.

247
00:15:38,813 --> 00:15:39,731
Seems fun.

248
00:15:40,231 --> 00:15:41,691
Let's eat!

249
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:43,610
-Let's eat!
-Let's eat!

250
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:45,445
Yummy.

251
00:15:45,528 --> 00:15:48,823
Eating together. Just being together.

252
00:15:53,912 --> 00:15:56,873
-Family always sticks together.
-Family always sticks together.

253
00:15:58,124 --> 00:15:59,167
-Oh!
-Oh!

254
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,169
We could use that.

255
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:09,678
FAMILY STICKS TOGETHER IN GOOD TIMES

256
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:10,929
You like it?

257
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:14,641
Mm-hmm.

258
00:16:14,724 --> 00:16:15,725
Impressive.

259
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:18,478
And for that,

260
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:21,523
here's your reward.

261
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:25,026
Thank you.

262
00:16:32,367 --> 00:16:34,369
Nice. We can use that in TV ads.

263
00:16:39,791 --> 00:16:40,834
It's good.

264
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:53,179
And that is how
we make Burger City accessible

265
00:16:53,263 --> 00:16:55,140
to every Filipino family.

266
00:16:55,932 --> 00:16:59,269
Same as how they loved Cala Soda.

267
00:17:02,689 --> 00:17:04,065
Good work, good work.

268
00:17:04,566 --> 00:17:06,025
Good work.

269
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:09,988
Okay.

270
00:17:10,739 --> 00:17:12,532
Good job, Patricia. Congratulations.

271
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:14,159
Thank you, sir.

272
00:17:19,164 --> 00:17:20,081
Carlota.

273
00:17:22,542 --> 00:17:23,793
Is it your lunch break yet?

274
00:17:24,753 --> 00:17:25,837
Let's eat out.

275
00:17:26,254 --> 00:17:29,340
Uh, wait here. My boss just
asked me to do something.

276
00:17:29,924 --> 00:17:32,302
Are these the ones you're selling?

277
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:34,179
Offer it to your colleagues.

278
00:17:34,262 --> 00:17:36,639
Here's the report
the finance department gave me.

279
00:17:37,891 --> 00:17:39,559
Ask for the fourth-quarter report.

280
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:41,060
Okay. Will do.

281
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:44,898
What are you doing here?

282
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,358
We're going out to lunch.

283
00:17:49,778 --> 00:17:51,362
Why do you seem to avoid me?

284
00:17:52,322 --> 00:17:53,615
Haven't you…

285
00:17:54,115 --> 00:17:55,742
moved on?

286
00:17:58,161 --> 00:18:00,413
Don't flatter yourself.

287
00:18:00,497 --> 00:18:02,373
You really don't have
self-awareness, do you?

288
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:04,793
If I'm hurting,

289
00:18:04,876 --> 00:18:07,337
that's because you took
my daughter away from me.

290
00:18:07,962 --> 00:18:10,882
Do you really think I still care
about you and this woman?

291
00:18:11,382 --> 00:18:14,469
I'm actually grateful
you're no longer in my life.

292
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:18,264
My life got better without you in it.

293
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,226
Don't worry.

294
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:25,021
My wife and daughter won't be here long.

295
00:18:26,147 --> 00:18:27,440
I have a business now.

296
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:29,400
Big time.

297
00:18:30,443 --> 00:18:31,945
Would you like to buy some?

298
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:33,488
This'll clear your impurities.

299
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:34,989
Seems like it's not working on you.

300
00:18:35,406 --> 00:18:37,575
I hope it's serious this time.

301
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:41,037
That's why I can't stand you.

302
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:42,664
That's just how you are.

303
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:47,043
All you do is belittle people!

304
00:18:47,377 --> 00:18:49,420
I was just thinking about Patricia.

305
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:54,759
For once, my daughter can finally rest
from looking after you both.

306
00:18:54,843 --> 00:18:56,135
What did you just say?

307
00:18:56,427 --> 00:18:58,972
Wait a minute! That's enough!

308
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:01,891
You're so hot headed.

309
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:07,397
You're furious, aren't you,
because nobody loves you?

310
00:19:08,857 --> 00:19:11,901
I'm sure you're jealous because…

311
00:19:12,986 --> 00:19:15,071
my husband visited me.

312
00:19:16,364 --> 00:19:18,116
Husband? Why?

313
00:19:18,575 --> 00:19:19,659
Are you guys married?

314
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:37,510
Here's your order.

315
00:19:40,722 --> 00:19:42,557
Why are you mad?

316
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:44,309
Are you that hungry?

317
00:19:46,394 --> 00:19:48,271
I feel so annoyed.

318
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:51,816
Do you not like the food?

319
00:19:54,319 --> 00:19:56,821
Why don't you marry me yet?

320
00:20:00,283 --> 00:20:01,951
Where is this coming from?

321
00:20:02,035 --> 00:20:04,579
You've been annulled with Diana
for a long time, right?

322
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:08,541
But you've never even asked me
to marry you.

323
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,628
Martin, we've already had two kids!

324
00:20:13,004 --> 00:20:14,756
Didn't you say that…

325
00:20:16,507 --> 00:20:18,384
you wanted an extravagant wedding?

326
00:20:19,594 --> 00:20:21,054
I can't give that to you yet.

327
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:23,264
Yes, you can!

328
00:20:24,098 --> 00:20:25,725
We need to save a bit more

329
00:20:25,808 --> 00:20:27,518
so I can give you what you want.

330
00:20:28,061 --> 00:20:29,520
An extravagant wedding.

331
00:20:36,069 --> 00:20:38,863
With… With a beautiful gown?

332
00:20:38,947 --> 00:20:42,700
And with a 100-person guest list?

333
00:20:43,326 --> 00:20:45,453
And will the reception be in a hotel?

334
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:48,247
Yes.

335
00:20:49,624 --> 00:20:50,625
But in the meantime,

336
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,961
we need to save up first.

337
00:21:00,176 --> 00:21:03,179
That's all I need to hear.

338
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:05,056
Assurance.

339
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:29,872
RICARDO: JONATHAN MARTINEZ
HAS A REPORT ON YOU AGAIN.

340
00:21:39,007 --> 00:21:41,884
What else are the secrets of La Familia?

341
00:21:42,593 --> 00:21:45,388
What happened to Melinda Aragon?

342
00:21:45,471 --> 00:21:49,934
Where is Lucio Aragon's wife
and Diana's mother?

343
00:21:50,435 --> 00:21:53,396
Almost none of us
could find any information,

344
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:55,982
and there are no pictures
of her online either.

345
00:21:57,358 --> 00:22:00,778
-Even the former employees of La Familia
-It's for her. She might not have eaten.

346
00:22:00,862 --> 00:22:03,281
don't know anything about her.

347
00:22:03,614 --> 00:22:07,910
Is there any truth to the rumor
that Melinda Aragon disappeared

348
00:22:08,494 --> 00:22:12,832
because Don Lucio covered up
a family scandal at that time?

349
00:22:14,459 --> 00:22:18,379
Because his wife ran off with another man?

350
00:22:18,463 --> 00:22:20,923
What other secrets
is the Aragon family hiding?

351
00:22:21,007 --> 00:22:21,966
WHAT HAPPENED TO MELINDA ARAGON?

352
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:23,176
Let's go.

353
00:22:30,183 --> 00:22:32,560
UNKNOWN: THERE ARE NO SECRETS
THAT CANNOT BE REVEALED.

354
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:47,408
-What's going on?
-Ricardo… there's…

355
00:22:47,492 --> 00:22:48,993
someone is scaring me.

356
00:22:49,077 --> 00:22:50,620
They messaged--

357
00:22:50,703 --> 00:22:52,455
Enzo, someone is scaring me
through text messages!

358
00:22:52,538 --> 00:22:54,540
-It's there!
-Here? On your phone?

359
00:22:54,624 --> 00:22:56,626
-They're scaring me!
-Ah…

360
00:22:57,043 --> 00:22:58,127
Ah…

361
00:22:58,211 --> 00:22:59,962
-Oh my god!
-Which one here, Ms. D?

362
00:23:00,046 --> 00:23:02,715
It… It should be the last one.

363
00:23:02,799 --> 00:23:05,218
It's not here. I'll have
the IT Department look at this.

364
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:06,427
Please.

365
00:23:08,805 --> 00:23:10,765
Do you think he's telling the truth?

366
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:12,600
Even I'm shocked.

367
00:23:12,683 --> 00:23:15,061
Mind you, I know
all the gossip going around.

368
00:23:15,144 --> 00:23:16,938
I never heard of that before.

369
00:23:17,021 --> 00:23:20,608
That means Sir Lucio
is good at keeping secrets.

370
00:23:20,691 --> 00:23:23,945
Come to think of it,
no one knows about this.

371
00:23:24,612 --> 00:23:26,405
But do you think it's the truth?

372
00:23:26,864 --> 00:23:27,990
I don't know.

373
00:23:28,074 --> 00:23:29,117
Psst.

374
00:23:49,178 --> 00:23:52,765
Tell me, can I still recover the message?

375
00:23:52,849 --> 00:23:55,601
Unfortunately, it can't be recovered.

376
00:23:55,685 --> 00:23:58,020
They sent you a disappearing message.

377
00:23:58,104 --> 00:24:00,273
It means once that message
is read and disappears,

378
00:24:00,356 --> 00:24:01,649
it will be automatically deleted.

379
00:24:03,484 --> 00:24:04,610
Diana.

380
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:08,364
Are you sure someone messaged you?

381
00:24:08,698 --> 00:24:10,408
Of course! I even read it!

382
00:24:10,491 --> 00:24:11,868
I can't go wrong about it!

383
00:24:12,869 --> 00:24:16,539
The only thing we can do
is set up an archiving option

384
00:24:16,622 --> 00:24:18,499
so that this doesn't happen again.

385
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:21,169
I'll have this reported
to the police, Ms. D.

386
00:24:21,252 --> 00:24:22,712
They might be able to do something.

387
00:24:23,379 --> 00:24:24,755
I'll do it.

388
00:24:26,299 --> 00:24:28,676
Where's Patricia's table?

389
00:24:28,759 --> 00:24:30,011
Ah, here.

390
00:24:30,553 --> 00:24:31,804
You!

391
00:24:32,555 --> 00:24:34,599
-One of you messaged me.
-Diana.

392
00:24:35,766 --> 00:24:38,060
What message are you talking about?

393
00:24:38,144 --> 00:24:40,563
We argued earlier,
and now you're threatening me.

394
00:24:40,646 --> 00:24:42,231
Stop acting innocent!

395
00:24:42,565 --> 00:24:44,483
You are making a fuss without evidence.

396
00:24:44,567 --> 00:24:45,484
It's the truth!

397
00:24:45,568 --> 00:24:48,404
And why would
I message you? Are we friends?

398
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:50,573
You're both just liars!

399
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:52,617
Mom. Dad.

400
00:24:53,201 --> 00:24:55,620
Your mom is throwing
accusations at us again.

401
00:24:55,995 --> 00:24:57,663
-Leave us alone, Diana!
-It's the truth.

402
00:24:58,039 --> 00:24:59,749
We don't want to get involved with you.

403
00:25:00,374 --> 00:25:01,334
That's enough.

404
00:25:02,084 --> 00:25:04,045
-Mom.
-Hmm?

405
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:05,421
Let's go.

406
00:25:05,504 --> 00:25:06,589
Come on.

407
00:25:12,303 --> 00:25:14,847
I don't understand anything she said.

408
00:25:14,931 --> 00:25:16,724
What did she say?

409
00:25:16,807 --> 00:25:17,975
Carlota.

410
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:25,691
You don't have to do this.

411
00:25:25,983 --> 00:25:27,485
Benjie is here.

412
00:25:28,986 --> 00:25:29,862
Diana.

413
00:25:30,446 --> 00:25:32,365
You were threatened and scared.

414
00:25:32,907 --> 00:25:34,533
I can't leave you.

415
00:25:34,951 --> 00:25:36,369
I'll protect you.

416
00:25:37,245 --> 00:25:39,038
Do you believe me?

417
00:25:39,830 --> 00:25:40,998
Why wouldn't I?

418
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:45,795
You might think I'm losing my mind, like…

419
00:25:47,838 --> 00:25:49,507
Like what happened to my mom.

420
00:25:51,717 --> 00:25:53,928
That's what they want everyone to think.

421
00:25:55,554 --> 00:25:57,431
You might doubt everyone,

422
00:25:59,684 --> 00:26:00,518
but for me,

423
00:26:01,227 --> 00:26:03,980
I will always choose to believe you.

424
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:13,739
Your mom is truly going insane.

425
00:26:13,823 --> 00:26:16,409
She's blaming us for things
we've never done!

426
00:26:17,243 --> 00:26:20,830
She was just affected
by that Jonathan's report.

427
00:26:20,913 --> 00:26:24,333
Is that enough reason to blame us?

428
00:26:25,876 --> 00:26:27,628
You also engaged instead of ignoring it.

429
00:26:28,879 --> 00:26:30,339
You're blaming me?

430
00:26:30,423 --> 00:26:33,342
Your father and I were blamed.

431
00:26:35,011 --> 00:26:38,639
Patricia, you're just starting
to get to know your mother.

432
00:26:39,056 --> 00:26:41,684
There are a lot of things
you still don't know about her.

433
00:26:42,310 --> 00:26:43,686
Like what?

434
00:26:45,104 --> 00:26:47,064
I don't know. I don't care anymore.

435
00:26:48,441 --> 00:26:49,358
Dad?

436
00:26:50,318 --> 00:26:51,902
Don't think about it anymore.

437
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:53,612
Just let her be.

438
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:59,702
I just want to know
why Mom is being threatened.

439
00:27:01,203 --> 00:27:05,041
We don't know all
the nasty things she's done

440
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:07,001
for her to be nervous.

441
00:27:22,350 --> 00:27:24,560
Good thing Ricardo was there.

442
00:27:25,853 --> 00:27:27,605
You're putting a meaning to this.

443
00:27:27,688 --> 00:27:29,315
What's wrong with that?

444
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:33,402
You need to be protected,
and Ricardo is doing that for you.

445
00:27:33,486 --> 00:27:36,614
I can't think about him
like that, Nanny Cora.

446
00:27:36,697 --> 00:27:37,990
Especially now.

447
00:27:38,074 --> 00:27:40,826
I want to know who's doing this to me.

448
00:27:41,452 --> 00:27:43,496
Are you suspecting someone?

449
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:47,166
Whoever that person is,

450
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:50,753
has something to do with my past.

451
00:27:52,088 --> 00:27:53,589
They're coming after me.

452
00:28:35,214 --> 00:28:38,175
Thank you very much for the information
about Belinda Aragon.

453
00:28:38,509 --> 00:28:39,677
If that happens,

454
00:28:40,219 --> 00:28:43,389
it'll be the news of the century.

455
00:28:43,472 --> 00:28:46,434
But wait, why are you doing this?

456
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:50,229
Don't you work for Diana?

457
00:28:53,107 --> 00:28:54,316
Just do your job.

458
00:28:54,942 --> 00:28:56,902
Like we agreed.

459
00:28:57,653 --> 00:28:59,405
Follow all my orders.

460
00:29:04,827 --> 00:29:05,911
We need to talk.

461
00:29:07,371 --> 00:29:08,539
About everything
that's been happening lately.

462
00:29:08,622 --> 00:29:11,000
The threat against you,
the report about Mom.

463
00:29:11,417 --> 00:29:13,544
What? Aren't you wondering
why all this is happening now?

464
00:29:14,128 --> 00:29:16,547
We're already looking
for a solution, Teddy.

465
00:29:16,630 --> 00:29:17,715
Who's "we"?

466
00:29:18,007 --> 00:29:19,216
Ricardo again?

467
00:29:20,384 --> 00:29:23,804
All our problems started
when he came here.

468
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:27,266
He just got here, he juast showed up.

469
00:29:27,892 --> 00:29:29,518
You think you know him that well already?

470
00:29:29,602 --> 00:29:31,645
Don't you think you trust him too much?

471
00:29:31,729 --> 00:29:33,981
Oh, let's say you're right,

472
00:29:34,064 --> 00:29:35,441
but what's his motive?

473
00:29:35,983 --> 00:29:38,319
Even people I've known
for years are the same.

474
00:29:39,653 --> 00:29:42,907
Even my own flesh and blood
wants to destroy me.

475
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:45,993
Oh, just admit it, Teddy.

476
00:29:46,076 --> 00:29:48,704
You want to eliminate the person
who's protecting me

477
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:50,372
from everything.

478
00:29:50,456 --> 00:29:51,916
From people like you.

479
00:29:51,999 --> 00:29:55,044
You only know him
within the four walls of La Familia.

480
00:29:55,628 --> 00:29:58,547
But you don't know him
outside the company.

481
00:29:58,631 --> 00:29:59,757
Come on!

482
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:03,302
Oh, I would be very interested, Teddy,

483
00:30:04,011 --> 00:30:08,057
if I knew you had no motive
behind everything you're telling me.

484
00:30:10,434 --> 00:30:11,644
See.

485
00:30:12,436 --> 00:30:13,771
I rest my case.

486
00:30:14,188 --> 00:30:16,482
You decide. But let me just tell you this.

487
00:30:16,565 --> 00:30:19,527
That trust is making you soft…

488
00:30:20,027 --> 00:30:21,111
Ms. Diana Aragon.

489
00:30:38,754 --> 00:30:39,797
Ricardo.

490
00:30:42,299 --> 00:30:44,301
Oh, Allan, how are you?

491
00:30:44,718 --> 00:30:46,220
When did you get back to the Philippines?

492
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:50,474
I came home for good
so I could be with my kids.

493
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:54,728
I heard you're working at La Familia now?

494
00:30:55,145 --> 00:30:56,939
Word travels fast, huh?

495
00:30:58,023 --> 00:31:00,067
Why did you want to meet with me?

496
00:31:00,526 --> 00:31:01,944
I found out

497
00:31:02,027 --> 00:31:04,697
because someone who also works
at La Familia talked to me.

498
00:31:05,155 --> 00:31:06,949
I thought they were a headhunter.

499
00:31:07,449 --> 00:31:09,702
But they just asked me about you.

500
00:31:10,828 --> 00:31:14,915
I thought maybe you could
get me into La Familia.

501
00:31:16,667 --> 00:31:18,252
Put in a good word for me?

502
00:31:20,671 --> 00:31:21,755
Who talked to you?

503
00:31:22,172 --> 00:31:24,341
Diana Aragon's brother.

504
00:31:24,842 --> 00:31:26,093
Oh, what's wrong with him?

505
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:28,220
-What's wrong with him?
-Yes, what's wrong with him?

506
00:31:28,721 --> 00:31:29,930
Teddy Aragon.

507
00:31:40,608 --> 00:31:41,859
Do you need help?

508
00:31:43,277 --> 00:31:45,154
No. I got this.

509
00:31:45,487 --> 00:31:46,488
What's that for?

510
00:31:47,156 --> 00:31:48,407
It's just for the activation.

511
00:31:49,575 --> 00:31:50,451
Good luck.

512
00:31:51,493 --> 00:31:52,411
Good luck to you too.

513
00:31:54,496 --> 00:31:55,789
Good luck to us.

514
00:31:56,582 --> 00:31:59,793
I hope our Burger City project
is a success.

515
00:32:01,837 --> 00:32:02,838
I hope so too,

516
00:32:02,921 --> 00:32:05,132
if Ricardo doesn't screw things up.

517
00:32:11,847 --> 00:32:13,015
What do you mean?

518
00:32:14,642 --> 00:32:17,811
I know you guys trust that bastard a lot.

519
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:20,731
But there's a lot you don't know.

520
00:32:21,815 --> 00:32:23,984
Did you and Sir Ricardo fight again?

521
00:32:24,818 --> 00:32:27,237
If so, can you please leave me out of it?

522
00:32:27,321 --> 00:32:28,614
I already have so much on my mind.

523
00:32:28,697 --> 00:32:30,574
I'm just warning you.

524
00:32:30,908 --> 00:32:33,118
You know what, thanks for the warning.

525
00:32:33,827 --> 00:32:35,996
But let's be honest.

526
00:32:36,664 --> 00:32:38,874
After everything you've done to me,

527
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:41,585
you're the one
I have a harder time trusting.

528
00:32:48,384 --> 00:32:49,718
Sir, let's go.

529
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:51,595
All right.

530
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:57,559
I already warned you, okay?

531
00:32:58,644 --> 00:33:00,020
It's up to you now.

532
00:33:01,605 --> 00:33:02,606
Excuse me.

533
00:33:22,459 --> 00:33:24,169
Oh, are you done?

534
00:33:24,670 --> 00:33:26,004
Can we continue reviewing?

535
00:33:26,088 --> 00:33:28,006
Not yet. Just wait. I still have…

536
00:33:28,549 --> 00:33:30,759
…something to send for Burger City.

537
00:33:31,385 --> 00:33:32,553
You're nervous, huh?

538
00:33:34,263 --> 00:33:35,681
I'm hungry.

539
00:33:36,098 --> 00:33:37,891
I have so much to take care of.

540
00:33:38,308 --> 00:33:39,977
This project at Burger City,

541
00:33:40,853 --> 00:33:44,690
then I'm also helping out
with my father's business.

542
00:33:44,773 --> 00:33:46,483
I still have a lot of orders
for toasted siopao,

543
00:33:46,567 --> 00:33:48,193
and then we have to review.

544
00:33:49,778 --> 00:33:51,530
So, can you still review?

545
00:33:52,489 --> 00:33:53,532
Hey.

546
00:33:53,907 --> 00:33:55,534
You can't give up, okay?

547
00:33:56,076 --> 00:33:57,786
I've never given up, not even once.

548
00:33:58,036 --> 00:34:00,748
My family's counting on this. I know that.

549
00:34:01,081 --> 00:34:03,041
That's why sometimes I wonder…

550
00:34:04,835 --> 00:34:07,755
…what if I put my studies on hold again?

551
00:34:08,130 --> 00:34:12,718
Wouldn't it be better if I let
my siblings finish school first?

552
00:34:12,801 --> 00:34:15,637
That way, I can help more
with my father's business

553
00:34:15,721 --> 00:34:18,557
and do my job at La Familia properly.

554
00:34:22,436 --> 00:34:23,896
Oh, my notebook!

555
00:34:23,979 --> 00:34:25,272
Where's my notebook? Is it there?

556
00:34:25,689 --> 00:34:26,774
Where did I put it?

557
00:34:26,857 --> 00:34:28,275
It was just here.

558
00:34:29,610 --> 00:34:30,861
Hmm.

559
00:34:34,448 --> 00:34:36,366
You're pretty careless, huh?

560
00:34:42,873 --> 00:34:44,541
But you're a good person, Patricia.

561
00:34:46,543 --> 00:34:48,420
Your family is lucky to have you.

562
00:34:49,630 --> 00:34:52,424
But I feel like
you need to admit to yourself

563
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:54,718
that you're struggling.

564
00:34:56,053 --> 00:34:59,306
So reviewing this
is the least of your priorities.

565
00:35:01,308 --> 00:35:04,061
I'm not. I can still handle it.

566
00:35:14,530 --> 00:35:16,782
That's why you put off reviewing,

567
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:19,952
because you feel like it's for you.

568
00:35:24,748 --> 00:35:26,124
You feel guilty…

569
00:35:27,292 --> 00:35:29,461
for doing something for yourself.

570
00:35:36,385 --> 00:35:39,680
You have to save some time
for yourself, Patricia.

571
00:35:40,389 --> 00:35:43,392
Because if you always put
other people first,

572
00:35:44,226 --> 00:35:46,061
you'll eventually run out of yourself.

573
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:48,564
And when you're all drained,

574
00:35:48,897 --> 00:35:51,024
what will you have left to give someone?

575
00:35:54,236 --> 00:35:56,363
Okay, I'll review now.

576
00:35:57,823 --> 00:35:58,782
Don't cry anymore.

577
00:35:58,866 --> 00:36:00,492
-It's because of you.
-Oh, why me?

578
00:36:00,576 --> 00:36:02,536
You called me careless.

579
00:36:02,619 --> 00:36:04,288
It's not like you can't take a joke.

580
00:36:04,371 --> 00:36:06,707
You know you're just hungry.

581
00:36:06,790 --> 00:36:09,001
You forget to eat. Eat first.

582
00:36:09,084 --> 00:36:10,168
Let's eat first, then we'll review.

583
00:36:10,252 --> 00:36:11,587
-Right?
-Yes, that's right.

584
00:36:20,470 --> 00:36:21,388
Teddy.

585
00:36:23,056 --> 00:36:25,058
Philip, from Business School. Remember?

586
00:36:25,142 --> 00:36:26,184
We were classmates.

587
00:36:28,312 --> 00:36:30,230
-How are you?
-I'm good.

588
00:36:30,564 --> 00:36:34,026
Congratulations, by the way,
on your venture with Burger City.

589
00:36:34,401 --> 00:36:35,444
Our biggest competitor!

590
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:37,905
-Yes!
-I'm from Big Bites.

591
00:36:37,988 --> 00:36:39,031
Oh.

592
00:36:39,114 --> 00:36:40,365
The collaboration between

593
00:36:40,449 --> 00:36:42,200
La Familia and Burger City
looks great, doesn't it?

594
00:36:42,534 --> 00:36:44,036
I'm sure you're going
to give us a hard time

595
00:36:44,119 --> 00:36:45,871
as business competitors.

596
00:36:46,747 --> 00:36:48,624
To be honest,

597
00:36:48,999 --> 00:36:51,126
I think the news is already
all over the business world.

598
00:36:51,835 --> 00:36:54,421
What happened to you
and your reassignment.

599
00:36:55,964 --> 00:36:57,257
I feel sorry for you.

600
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:00,302
Well…

601
00:37:02,596 --> 00:37:04,264
I don't need your pity.

602
00:37:04,681 --> 00:37:05,599
Excuse me.

603
00:37:05,682 --> 00:37:08,936
What if I told you I can
give you what you need?

604
00:37:09,645 --> 00:37:11,146
What do you mean?

605
00:37:12,981 --> 00:37:17,569
You shouldn't make La Familia
a dead end for you, Teddy.

606
00:37:18,195 --> 00:37:20,322
There are a lot of options out there.

607
00:37:20,864 --> 00:37:22,449
Just like our company.

608
00:37:23,033 --> 00:37:26,787
As a former classmate and a friend,

609
00:37:28,121 --> 00:37:29,539
I can help you.

610
00:37:36,797 --> 00:37:39,049
Waiter. Two, please.

611
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:42,469
All right. I'm listening.

612
00:38:12,332 --> 00:38:13,834
I love my life.

613
00:38:14,626 --> 00:38:16,378
I love my life.

614
00:38:17,004 --> 00:38:18,380
I love my life.

615
00:38:28,265 --> 00:38:30,392
Are you nervous, Patricia?

616
00:38:32,519 --> 00:38:33,603
Enzo!

617
00:38:35,272 --> 00:38:36,648
What are you wearing?

618
00:38:36,732 --> 00:38:38,025
You're so red.

619
00:38:38,108 --> 00:38:40,569
Red is a lucky color to wear for an exam.

620
00:38:40,652 --> 00:38:42,612
-Don't you know that?
-Ah…

621
00:38:43,405 --> 00:38:44,364
Sure.

622
00:38:46,700 --> 00:38:48,326
Wait a minute. What are you doing here?

623
00:38:48,410 --> 00:38:51,538
I'm here to make sure you take the exam.

624
00:38:54,583 --> 00:38:57,836
Oh, I have a good luck charm for you.

625
00:39:05,052 --> 00:39:06,178
Here.

626
00:39:06,887 --> 00:39:08,930
A pencil I sharpened myself.

627
00:39:09,514 --> 00:39:10,974
Use this for your exam.

628
00:39:12,100 --> 00:39:16,063
Because they say someone taking an exam

629
00:39:16,146 --> 00:39:19,066
should use a pencil that was sharpened by…

630
00:39:21,401 --> 00:39:23,070
an intelligent person.

631
00:39:23,528 --> 00:39:25,155
Oh, boy!

632
00:39:25,238 --> 00:39:27,240
-Unbelievable!
-Mm-hmm.

633
00:39:27,324 --> 00:39:28,533
Right?

634
00:39:33,914 --> 00:39:35,290
Good morning.

635
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:37,542
Please proceed inside for the exam.

636
00:39:42,798 --> 00:39:43,840
Hey.

637
00:39:43,924 --> 00:39:45,801
Don't be nervous.

638
00:39:45,884 --> 00:39:49,096
You prepared for this. Okay? You got this.

639
00:39:49,638 --> 00:39:50,847
Go ahead.

640
00:40:13,870 --> 00:40:16,331
"Good luck on your exam. You've got this."

641
00:40:28,969 --> 00:40:30,720
Where's Diana?

642
00:40:30,804 --> 00:40:33,890
-Mr. Borja, Diana isn't here.
-She has a meeting off-site.

643
00:40:33,974 --> 00:40:35,767
How could you let this happen, Ricardo?

644
00:40:36,143 --> 00:40:38,061
They copied our project almost exactly.

645
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:39,729
There might have been a leak.

646
00:40:40,522 --> 00:40:43,358
Leak? You better get
to the bottom of this.

647
00:40:46,736 --> 00:40:47,571
A leak?

648
00:40:47,654 --> 00:40:49,406
What happened?

649
00:40:49,865 --> 00:40:51,366
Here, take a look.

650
00:41:14,055 --> 00:41:16,057
The entire campaign is canceled.

651
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:24,900
But we shouldn't stop looking
for whoever leaked the campaign.

652
00:41:25,775 --> 00:41:27,110
I'll take care of it.

653
00:41:28,069 --> 00:41:30,197
Whoever did this is going to pay.

654
00:41:31,531 --> 00:41:33,992
I'll destroy them. All of them!

655
00:41:34,618 --> 00:41:36,244
Mark my words.

656
00:41:37,704 --> 00:41:39,664
Whoever did it,

657
00:41:40,457 --> 00:41:44,961
they're going to regret the day
they decided to cross me.

658
00:41:50,425 --> 00:41:51,259
Hey, Genevieve!

659
00:41:51,343 --> 00:41:54,346
There's one more concept
that needs a deck.

660
00:41:54,429 --> 00:41:55,680
Isn't it done yet?

661
00:41:55,764 --> 00:41:57,432
Double-check all the data, okay?

662
00:41:57,515 --> 00:41:58,808
We have no room for errors.

663
00:41:58,892 --> 00:42:00,769
-Yes, sir.
-Everyone, listen up!

664
00:42:00,852 --> 00:42:02,854
We have to make this work, okay?

665
00:42:02,938 --> 00:42:05,774
I want everyone to give it their all.

666
00:42:05,857 --> 00:42:06,816
Okay?

667
00:42:06,900 --> 00:42:08,568
-Let's get to work!
-Yes, sir.

668
00:42:08,652 --> 00:42:13,240
This concept highlights transparency
and community engagement.

669
00:42:13,323 --> 00:42:14,407
So, what do you think?

670
00:42:15,116 --> 00:42:17,160
I don't know about you, but I, uh…

671
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:19,246
I found it all a bit underwhelming.

672
00:42:19,329 --> 00:42:21,915
If it doesn't work for you,
we have other options.

673
00:42:21,998 --> 00:42:23,708
-Mm-hmm?
-Diana made sure of it.

674
00:42:28,338 --> 00:42:30,882
Oops! You can't doze off!

675
00:42:30,966 --> 00:42:33,260
Coffee, guys! Sir Enzo's treat!

676
00:42:33,343 --> 00:42:34,177
Thank you, Lala.

677
00:42:34,636 --> 00:42:37,973
Hannah, here are
the historical files we need.

678
00:42:38,056 --> 00:42:39,683
See if we can use anything from these.

679
00:42:57,367 --> 00:42:58,994
Hey, any news?

680
00:42:59,369 --> 00:43:01,037
Your exam results
are coming out today, right?

681
00:43:02,789 --> 00:43:05,000
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Relax.

682
00:43:05,083 --> 00:43:06,918
Breathe, okay?

683
00:43:07,002 --> 00:43:08,211
You got this.

684
00:43:08,295 --> 00:43:10,088
You're going to pass. I'm sure of it.

685
00:43:11,047 --> 00:43:12,716
Keep me posted, okay?

686
00:43:17,679 --> 00:43:19,514
Is that it?

687
00:43:20,515 --> 00:43:21,433
Take a look.

688
00:43:22,225 --> 00:43:23,601
Enzo…

689
00:43:24,311 --> 00:43:25,228
What's wrong?

690
00:43:25,312 --> 00:43:27,689
Let's open it together.

691
00:43:27,772 --> 00:43:29,399
-Okay?
-Okay.

692
00:43:29,482 --> 00:43:30,817
-Ready?
-Okay.

693
00:43:33,695 --> 00:43:35,530
"We are pleased to inform you

694
00:43:35,864 --> 00:43:38,908
that you qualify to be admitted

695
00:43:38,992 --> 00:43:41,661
for the continuing education program."

696
00:43:41,745 --> 00:43:42,912
-You passed!
-I passed!

697
00:43:42,996 --> 00:43:45,081
You passed!

698
00:43:45,165 --> 00:43:47,000
I knew it! I knew it!

699
00:43:49,461 --> 00:43:52,130
You passed, Patricia!
You did it! You did it!

700
00:43:58,553 --> 00:43:59,846
Congratulations, Patricia.

701
00:44:01,556 --> 00:44:04,059
I knew you could do it

702
00:44:05,477 --> 00:44:06,936
I'm so proud of you.

703
00:44:07,354 --> 00:44:08,813
Thank you.

704
00:44:08,897 --> 00:44:10,732
Thank you, Enzo.

705
00:44:11,608 --> 00:44:13,777
So something good
can still happen in my life.

706
00:44:13,860 --> 00:44:15,904
-I told you.
-Thanks for believing in me.

707
00:44:17,739 --> 00:44:19,366
It was all worth it!

708
00:44:19,449 --> 00:44:21,284
-How do we do it again?
-Like this?

709
00:44:21,368 --> 00:44:23,787
-Like this, not like that!
-Oh, it isn't!

710
00:44:25,413 --> 00:44:26,456
Good job!

711
00:44:28,166 --> 00:44:30,377
Dad? Mom?

712
00:44:30,710 --> 00:44:32,337
I'm home!

713
00:44:40,887 --> 00:44:42,389
April! Jena!

714
00:44:42,931 --> 00:44:43,807
April!

715
00:44:44,933 --> 00:44:46,935
Dad! Mom!

716
00:44:50,563 --> 00:44:52,941
-Go on, eat up.
-Are you having fun?

717
00:44:53,274 --> 00:44:55,443
-Do you like the food?
-It's delicious.

718
00:44:55,902 --> 00:44:58,321
Eat up, okay?

719
00:44:58,405 --> 00:44:59,864
Mm. Wait a sec.

720
00:45:03,118 --> 00:45:04,244
It's Patricia.

721
00:45:04,702 --> 00:45:06,496
-Hello?
-Dad?

722
00:45:06,996 --> 00:45:08,123
Dad, where are you?

723
00:45:08,415 --> 00:45:11,376
I'm eating out
with your mother and your sisters.

724
00:45:11,459 --> 00:45:12,460
Are you home already?

725
00:45:12,544 --> 00:45:15,839
Your mother said you'd be home late.

726
00:45:15,922 --> 00:45:17,048
I see.

727
00:45:18,258 --> 00:45:21,261
Okay, Dad. I'll see you at home.

728
00:45:22,345 --> 00:45:24,931
Martin, do that later.
The food's getting cold.

729
00:45:25,014 --> 00:45:26,141
You should eat.

730
00:45:26,224 --> 00:45:28,268
We'll bring home some food for you, okay?

731
00:45:28,810 --> 00:45:29,853
Bye.

732
00:45:31,729 --> 00:45:33,273
Okay, Dad. Enjoy.

733
00:45:34,190 --> 00:45:35,233
Bye.

734
00:46:05,513 --> 00:46:07,599
"Solo celebration."

735
00:46:23,406 --> 00:46:25,074
I still have so much work to do.

736
00:46:25,158 --> 00:46:27,076
What are we doing here?

737
00:46:27,160 --> 00:46:28,745
Is this your solution?

738
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:31,956
When you're too focused,

739
00:46:32,499 --> 00:46:34,626
you can't see the whole picture.

740
00:46:36,211 --> 00:46:37,712
Just take a step back.

741
00:46:39,005 --> 00:46:40,673
Then you'll see the whole picture.

742
00:46:42,258 --> 00:46:43,510
You'll find a solution.

743
00:46:43,593 --> 00:46:44,677
Come on.

744
00:47:09,494 --> 00:47:10,787
Wow.

745
00:47:11,371 --> 00:47:12,288
Wow.

746
00:47:49,450 --> 00:47:50,618
Are you okay?

747
00:47:50,702 --> 00:47:52,412
-I'm okay.
-Okay!

748
00:47:52,495 --> 00:47:54,080
Yes. All right. You're good.

749
00:48:23,818 --> 00:48:26,321
MS. D, I PASSED THE EXAM

750
00:49:17,580 --> 00:49:18,623
Enzo?

751
00:49:22,669 --> 00:49:24,587
-Hi.
-What are you doing here?

752
00:49:25,421 --> 00:49:27,256
I heard there was a celebration here.

753
00:49:28,466 --> 00:49:29,634
Oh, wow.

754
00:49:29,717 --> 00:49:31,094
You're something else, huh?

755
00:49:31,177 --> 00:49:33,471
You went here just to celebrate with me?

756
00:49:33,805 --> 00:49:35,223
Why not?

757
00:49:35,306 --> 00:49:37,225
This is a big deal for you.

758
00:49:37,934 --> 00:49:39,977
It's only right that we celebrate it…

759
00:49:46,567 --> 00:49:47,777
…the right way.

760
00:49:51,364 --> 00:49:52,865
What's the "right way" of celebrating?

761
00:49:53,449 --> 00:49:55,952
I know a perfect place for that.

762
00:49:56,577 --> 00:49:58,162
-Come on.
-Hold on!

763
00:50:03,251 --> 00:50:04,419
Hold on.

764
00:50:04,502 --> 00:50:05,837
Give me five minutes.

765
00:50:11,092 --> 00:50:12,635
-Almost there.
-My goodness.

766
00:50:12,719 --> 00:50:14,554
-Careful. To your left.
-Where are we?

767
00:50:15,012 --> 00:50:16,848
-Are we there yet?
-Okay.

768
00:50:16,931 --> 00:50:18,391
We're almost there. And…

769
00:50:19,016 --> 00:50:21,060
Three, two, one…

770
00:50:21,436 --> 00:50:22,520
Surprise!

771
00:50:24,814 --> 00:50:26,941
Oh, wow!

772
00:50:27,024 --> 00:50:29,235
-You like it?
-It looks great!

773
00:50:29,736 --> 00:50:30,737
Look.

774
00:50:30,820 --> 00:50:32,405
I blew all the balloons up myself.

775
00:50:32,488 --> 00:50:34,157
Seriously?!

776
00:50:34,741 --> 00:50:35,658
This is too much!

777
00:50:35,742 --> 00:50:38,494
It's as if I graduated Magna Cum Laude!

778
00:50:38,578 --> 00:50:39,454
Have a seat.

779
00:50:40,580 --> 00:50:42,999
I have another surprise for you.

780
00:50:44,709 --> 00:50:46,210
Here.

781
00:51:01,434 --> 00:51:03,019
Enzo, I can't take this.

782
00:51:03,436 --> 00:51:04,854
That's for you.

783
00:51:05,897 --> 00:51:07,315
That will help you.

784
00:51:08,024 --> 00:51:12,278
You can't use the company's laptop
for your online classes, right?

785
00:51:12,361 --> 00:51:13,613
So, I got you that.

786
00:51:14,280 --> 00:51:15,448
You can use that.

787
00:51:16,365 --> 00:51:17,617
And hello!

788
00:51:17,700 --> 00:51:18,576
Look.

789
00:51:19,577 --> 00:51:21,621
This is where I got the money to buy that.

790
00:51:21,704 --> 00:51:22,872
I emptied the jar.

791
00:51:22,955 --> 00:51:25,625
With all your wrong answers,
I was able to buy a tablet.

792
00:51:25,958 --> 00:51:27,460
-Can you believe that?
-Unbelievable.

793
00:51:27,543 --> 00:51:29,712
You really tend to overreact, huh?

794
00:51:29,796 --> 00:51:33,049
There are more coins in the jar
for my correct answers.

795
00:51:33,132 --> 00:51:35,009
Okay, fine. You win.

796
00:51:35,092 --> 00:51:37,595
I added a little more so I could buy that.

797
00:51:37,678 --> 00:51:39,680
Don't worry about paying me back for that.

798
00:51:40,097 --> 00:51:42,058
Consider that a gift.

799
00:51:53,277 --> 00:51:55,571
Hey. Why are you crying?

800
00:52:00,159 --> 00:52:01,244
This is nice.

801
00:52:05,206 --> 00:52:06,791
Thank you.

802
00:52:08,292 --> 00:52:11,379
You're the only person
who made this occasion special for me.

803
00:52:21,848 --> 00:52:25,309
You know what I learned
when my parents died?

804
00:52:27,979 --> 00:52:30,189
That if you're prepared
for life's challenges,

805
00:52:31,190 --> 00:52:34,944
you should also be prepared
to enjoy life's joys.

806
00:52:37,321 --> 00:52:38,656
Hmm.

807
00:53:09,478 --> 00:53:10,605
Thank you for doing this.

808
00:53:12,857 --> 00:53:14,317
You're welcome.

809
00:53:16,861 --> 00:53:18,946
What's wrong? You seem sad.

810
00:53:21,574 --> 00:53:23,951
No one's ever done this for me before.

811
00:53:26,120 --> 00:53:28,289
Why are you so good to me, Ricardo?

812
00:53:34,086 --> 00:53:35,838
Because I like you, Diana.

813
00:53:42,720 --> 00:53:43,971
I'm sorry.

814
00:53:44,639 --> 00:53:46,474
I can't do this.

815
00:53:49,602 --> 00:53:51,354
I'm not ready yet.

816
00:53:54,065 --> 00:53:55,399
I understand.

817
00:53:56,233 --> 00:53:57,944
But I'm not Martin.

818
00:53:58,778 --> 00:54:00,404
I won't lie to you.

819
00:54:02,531 --> 00:54:04,116
I won't hurt you.

820
00:54:31,894 --> 00:54:34,021
Did you meet up with Ricardo?

821
00:54:34,772 --> 00:54:36,148
How did you know?

822
00:54:36,649 --> 00:54:38,609
You're smiling.

823
00:54:38,693 --> 00:54:41,988
He's the only person I know
who can make you smile.

824
00:54:46,242 --> 00:54:47,702
Nanny, please.

825
00:54:48,953 --> 00:54:51,205
You know what I've gone through.

826
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:55,376
I don't know
if I can trust again just yet.

827
00:54:55,459 --> 00:54:57,962
Well, how sure are you

828
00:54:58,462 --> 00:55:01,090
that you're going to get hurt again?

829
00:55:01,424 --> 00:55:03,884
Well, isn't that my life's theme?

830
00:55:04,719 --> 00:55:08,305
Diana, we've been together for years.

831
00:55:09,640 --> 00:55:11,934
I've seen all the times

832
00:55:12,018 --> 00:55:15,688
you built La Familia from the ground.

833
00:55:17,314 --> 00:55:19,483
But when it comes to yourself,

834
00:55:19,942 --> 00:55:21,235
why are you full of doubt?

835
00:55:23,529 --> 00:55:27,700
I can see how Ricardo takes care of you.

836
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:30,036
He puts you first.

837
00:55:30,995 --> 00:55:33,581
He cares for you.

838
00:55:35,291 --> 00:55:36,417
Diana…

839
00:55:37,084 --> 00:55:38,919
it's time to take care of yourself too.

840
00:55:46,260 --> 00:55:50,014
Give yourself a chance to love again.

841
00:55:54,226 --> 00:55:57,063
I've got Diana wrapped around my finger.

842
00:55:57,772 --> 00:55:59,732
It's only a matter of time…

843
00:56:00,900 --> 00:56:03,652
before she falls in love with me.

844
00:56:03,736 --> 00:56:05,821
And she won't be able to escape.

845
00:56:12,870 --> 00:56:14,038
Please don't tell Ms. D about this.

846
00:56:14,121 --> 00:56:15,372
I don't want any special treatment.

847
00:56:15,456 --> 00:56:17,500
-Patricia! Patricia!
-What happened?

848
00:56:17,583 --> 00:56:19,210
I have to take care of my daughter.

849
00:56:19,293 --> 00:56:20,628
What is this? A family reunion?

850
00:56:20,711 --> 00:56:23,172
You're both going to take care
of your beloved daughter?

851
00:56:23,255 --> 00:56:26,425
Did you come here for me or for Patricia?

852
00:56:26,509 --> 00:56:27,968
I'm just worried about Patricia.

853
00:56:28,052 --> 00:56:29,512
-Why?
-I like her, Ms. D.

854
00:56:29,595 --> 00:56:32,014
I know you're behind all of this!
You set me up!

855
00:56:32,098 --> 00:56:34,183
What would happen to us
if you get kicked out of La Familia?

856
00:56:34,266 --> 00:56:36,060
The more she lets me into her life,

857
00:56:36,143 --> 00:56:37,353
the more I can ruin her.

858
00:56:37,436 --> 00:56:39,814
I will make sure
she loses everything she has.
